{"3209690":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"808","steam_appid":3209690,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3209690\/extras\/7f74e49bc95af004f683dfea8f99222a.avif?t=1782166809\" width=600 height=225 \/><\/span><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>You wake up in a padded cell with no memory of how you got there. A voice in your ear says his name is Dex. He's going to help you remember.<\/strong><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the game<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ash is a patient at Helix Industries, a corporation that resolves traumatic experiences. Across 808 days of therapy, your operator Dex guides you through your own past memories: An art gallery you don't remember visiting, a tabletop fantasy game you don't remember playing, a restaurant where someone never arrived to meet you, a cabin in the snow you used to call home.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >808 is a first-person narrative game in the tradition of <strong>The Stanley Parable<\/strong>, <strong>The Beginner's Guide<\/strong>, and <strong>Firewatch<\/strong>. The game is played by walking, looking, listening, observing, carefully. The relationship between Ash and Dex is the core of the experience.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1–1:30 hours<\/strong> of single-player narrative<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fully voice-acted<\/strong> dialogue between two central characters<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>14 distinct memory environments<\/strong>, each with its own mechanics, drawing in 3D space, rolling dice against a dragon, raking a zen garden, waiting at a table that won't be filled<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A diegetic UI overlay<\/strong> that tells you things the dialogue won't<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Branching dialogue<\/strong> that shapes the tone of your relationship with Dex<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One ending<\/strong>. The kind you carry with you.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Memories are what makes you, you.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By the end, you will understand what happened to you, and what is still happening, and what has been happening for longer than you knew.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a quiet game. It is not a horror game in the way that word is usually used. But it is, in its own way, the most unsettling thing we know how to make.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p>","about_the_game":"<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3209690\/extras\/7f74e49bc95af004f683dfea8f99222a.avif?t=1782166809\" width=600 height=225 \/><\/span><\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" style=\"text-align: center\"><strong>You wake up in a padded cell with no memory of how you got there. A voice in your ear says his name is Dex. He's going to help you remember.<\/strong><\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About the game<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Ash is a patient at Helix Industries, a corporation that resolves traumatic experiences. Across 808 days of therapy, your operator Dex guides you through your own past memories: An art gallery you don't remember visiting, a tabletop fantasy game you don't remember playing, a restaurant where someone never arrived to meet you, a cabin in the snow you used to call home.<\/p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >808 is a first-person narrative game in the tradition of <strong>The Stanley Parable<\/strong>, <strong>The Beginner's Guide<\/strong>, and <strong>Firewatch<\/strong>. The game is played by walking, looking, listening, observing, carefully. The relationship between Ash and Dex is the core of the experience.<\/p><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>1–1:30 hours<\/strong> of single-player narrative<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Fully voice-acted<\/strong> dialogue between two central characters<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>14 distinct memory environments<\/strong>, each with its own mechanics, drawing in 3D space, rolling dice against a dragon, raking a zen garden, waiting at a table that won't be filled<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>A diegetic UI overlay<\/strong> that tells you things the dialogue won't<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Branching dialogue<\/strong> that shapes the tone of your relationship with Dex<\/p><\/li><li><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>One ending<\/strong>. The kind you carry with you.<\/p><\/li><\/ul><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Memories are what makes you, you.<\/h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By the end, you will understand what happened to you, and what is still happening, and what has been happening for longer than you knew.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >This is a quiet game. It is not a horror game in the way that word is usually used. But it is, in its own way, the most unsettling thing we know how to make.<\/p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><\/p>","short_description":"808 explores the memories that define us and what happens when they're taken away. It's a surreal game about love, loss, and a difficult choice: the pain of authenticity, or the peace of self forgetfulness.","supported_languages":"영어<strong>*<\/strong><br><strong>*<\/strong>음성이 지원되는 언어","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3209690\/1ec4ad77709388de090d922c25cf105c817f0aca\/header.jpg?t=1782166809","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/3209690\/e363af46f8d39193b04f3ff951b01116d28d2450\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1782166809","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akama